@startbpmn BP19_KeepAnEditAsADraft
lang en             ' the only stakeholder is the Software Architect, who authored the sources in English

output L1 "01_detailed/BP19_KeepAnEditAsADraft.bpmn"
output L2 "02_detailed/BP19_KeepAnEditAsADraft.bpmn"

' Provenance (never in a drawn note, lint rule 5):
'   - unfinished input is a draft, forms and dialogs included, and no draft is version-controlled:
'     BR-121, SA 2026-10-10
'   - a draft survives abandoning the gesture, a crash and a restart, and changes nothing until the
'     gesture completes: BR-121
'   - keeping a draft is one-way: nothing waits for it to be kept: BR-121
'   - whichever write commits the input discards the draft it came from, so the discard belongs to
'     the committing process and is drawn there: BR-121
'   - where a draft is kept is not a business concern - it lives with the user's data and outside
'     version control, like the remembered interface state: BR-121, BR-92
'   - the particular draft rules instance this general one: a goal check-out sitting (BR-32), the
'     check-out notes (BR-37), a staged task batch (BR-63)
'
' Scope: EVERY draftable field in the product, drawn once. Until 2026-10-11 each editing process
' drew its own draft chain - eleven call sites realizing one operation - and the Software Architect
' ruled that out: "it would complicate editing text fields qualified for drafting in BPs", and
' "whenever I edit a draftable text field incl. a goal check-out field or a day note field, I want
' to apply the drafting BP". So the operation is drawn here, once, and every editing process binds
' BR-121 to the step that fills the field instead of drawing a chain of its own. The retired call
' sites are BP03.08, BP04.04, BP05.16, BP06.09, BP07.02, BP11.10, BP12.09, BP13.02, BP16.08,
' BP17.16 and BP18.09; their ids are never reused (ADR-066).
'
' A STAGED TASK BATCH is not this process. It is a draft in BR-121's sense, but the user picks it
' up, amends it, reorders it and commits it as a batch, which is work of its own: BP10, BR-63,
' SA 2026-10-11 ("draft tasks are completely different beast and are excluded here").
'
' WHICH fields are draftable is the owning process's business, not this drawing's: this one says
' what happens to any of them while it is being filled in.

' ===== The user: fills a field in, and is free to walk away from it =====
pool "User" {
  start "A draftable field is being filled in"
  :Type into the field;
  multiInstance
  rule BR-121
  send "Keep the edit as a draft" to draftIn
  note "Leaving it costs nothing: it is there on the next launch, half-finished, and it has changed nothing meanwhile. Committing it is the act of whichever process the field belongs to, and that is what discards the draft."
  end "The edit is safe either way"
}

' ===== The system: one chain, for every draftable field there is =====
system pool "Bearing" {
  messageStart "Edit submitted" as draftIn
  call "BP19.01_KeepTheEditAsADraft" "Keep the edit as a draft" {
    :Keep what is typed as a draft;
    rule BR-121
  }
  note "One-way: nothing waits for the draft to be kept. It stays out of the planning history, and nothing it describes takes effect until the gesture that owns it completes."
  end "Draft kept"
}

@endbpmn
